// This message file contains text to be used in game-supplied books.
// Only the message line numbers 1000 or higher are valid.
// Format: each line begins with a font number and justification letter,
// followed by the text for that line. Each line becomes a paragraph in
// the book.

// Some font numbers to use:
//	37  Book Type
//	497 Script
//	171 Old English
//	28  Mage Type

// Justification letters (you must use one)
//	l = left
//	c = center


{1000}{37l Test message line.}

{1010}{497l 	If you are reading this, then it is my hope that you are the one I sent for those many weeks ago, but if you are not, I hope you can still feel it in your heart to help me and my people, especially my daughter.
}
{1011}{497l		For you to understand what is happening here, it will be best for me to tell my tale from the beginning. This village has been a happy one for most of its existence. When our beloved king died, it was his wish that we leave the castle empty, as his monument. And so it was, for years following his demise.
}
{1012}{497l 	Some time ago, the winds changed, and an unease swept over the town. People began to disappear in the night. All our attempts to thwart whoever was invading our town as we slept came to naught. The local mage, after a fortnight of fasting and meditation, told us that the evil that had come upon us was living deep within our sacred castle. If calmer heads had not prevailed, the whole town would have besieged the castle that night. The first group of volunteers set out to destroy the evil that had come to dwell among us the next morning. They were never heard from again.
}
{1013}{497l		We have sent several groups since then, with none ever returning. The last of us will be going at first light, and my daughter is meant to be among us, but I cannot allow this. She is too precious to me to see her die. Find her, and keep her safe.
}
{1014}{497l		Please, help her, help us all.
}
{1015}{497l	Your friend,				
		
			Fernando}

{1020}{497l		My only hope is that friendly eyes are reading this. I have to chance leaving this in this place, as I fear my time is near. We are preparing for our final assault on the demonic mistress that has brought such terror on our village.
}

{1021}{497l		Somewhere in the village I once called home you will find a rather tame wolf. This is not a wolf, but in actuality, my daughter. She is under a spell I had the mage cast on her myself, in a misguided attempt to keep her safe. My fear is that she will now be condemned to live out her days in that bestial form. Please use the scroll of dispel magick I have hidden here with this book to return her to her beautiful human form.
}

{1022}{497l		Please help us. You are our only hope.

		Fernando}

{1030}{497l		The mistress has gone insane! I fear for my life every day, and I only do her bidding in a vain attempt to have my meager existence spared from the horrors she is capable of. I am writing this now so that perhaps someone, someday, will know I only helped her out of fear, though I will surely pay for my sins in the world to come. Please, pray for me...
}

{1031}{497l		The mistress has always been a cruel woman, beating her servants mercilessly, but at least we were being fed and clothed. Besides, most days she was too consumed with her petty delusions to pay us any mind. But that all changed when she beat Ursula mercilessly, and got her blood on her hands. She was then convinced that the spots that had been touched by blood had actually become younger. She felt she had discovered the secret to eternal youth in her servant's blood. She cut out Ursula's heart herself!
}

{1032}{497l		She began consuming her servants, one by one. I alone was spared, for what reason I do not know. When her servants were gone, she began taking local drunks, and when they were used up, she turned to the young women of the village. We barely escaped that place with our lives.
}

{1033}{497l		That is when we came to this place. To keep secure from angry villagers, she has sold herself to any number of demonic forces. I pray that I will be forgiven for my part in all this, by whatever powers there may be.}
